<!-- awf:section working-memory -->
## Working memory

A minimal simple fix uses no effort. Once work is a concrete non-minimal outcome, create or resume exactly one immutable slugged effort with `awf effort new "<outcome>"`; it always owns `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`. Carry the slug and exact path through checkpoints and handoffs, but verify checkpoint claims against repository sources and current-state documentation. One effort has one user-managed writer; report-only children and helpers never edit shared memory. Never create standalone memory, commit the owned file, or cite its concrete path in an ADR, plan, or commit message. Worktree-backed efforts integrate and remove topology after terminal review and before retrospective; retrospective finishes the effort last. The detailed protocol lives in the workflow doc's working-memory section.
<!-- awf:end -->

